  "id": "COMPOUND:26514 - PROTEIN:5794",
  "verbalization": "Cyanide is implicated in the relationship with LAPC4 through a series of molecular pathways involving the high-affinity choline transporter. The evidence suggests that Cyanide acts as a target of multiple compounds, including (2R,3S,4R,5R,6S)-2-[...]-triol, 24-Methylenecycloartanone, and 2-Methoxyjuglone, all of which are known to interact with the high-affinity choline transporter. These compounds are likely to modulate the transporter's function, potentially affecting its ability to transport choline and, by extension, influencing the cellular processes that LAPC4 is involved in. The presence of multiple targets at the choline transporter level indicates a possible mechanism by which Cyanide may exert its effects on LAPC4, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship and underscores the importance of further investigation into the molecular mechanisms linking Cyanide to LAPC4.",
